 of education reform in the 21st century is the cultivation of creativity and innovation. The traditional education system tends to stifle creativity by promoting conformity and standardization. However, in an increasingly dynamic and competitive global landscape, creativity and innovation are becoming highly valued skills. By incorporating art, music, drama, and other creative subjects into the curriculum, students can develop their creative thinking and problem-solving abilities. Furthermore, there needs to be a greater emphasis on lifelong learning and adaptability. The rapid pace of technological advancements means that the skills needed for the job market are constantly evolving. Therefore, education should not end at graduation but should foster a love for learning and provide individuals with the skills and mindset to adapt and learn throughout their lives. This can be achieved through the promotion of continuous professional development and the integration of lifelong learning programs into educational institutions. In conclusion, education reform in the 21st century should focus on critical thinking, the integration of technology, creativity, and adaptability. By shifting the focus from rote memorization to critical thinking and problem-solving skills, incorporating technology into the classroom, encouraging creativity, and promoting lifelong learning, education can better prepare individuals for the challenges of the modern world. These reforms will ensure that education remains relevant, equips individuals with the necessary skills, and enables them to succeed in a rapidly changing global landscape.", "encoded_message": "Pedagogy contains continuously occurred a single pivotal facet relating to the public, molding the intellects and destiny of people. During the 21st age, the requirement for tutoring amendment has evolve into obvious among perspective of the accelerated adjustments and progressions in IT, worldwide integration, and the transitioning deman